[
  "Welcome back to The Sound Above. I am Mike Hall. Today we enter The Human Communication Layer & Inclusion. Before code synthesis models and automated agents, developers met face to face to establish standards of craftsmanship. Today we rewatch Episode 17: Dave 'pragdave' Thomas from SCNA 2013 (2013).",
  "PragDave delivered one of the most provocative keynotes at SCNA Chicago, challenging attendees not to turn craftsmanship into a cult.",
  "What inspired the original Pragmatic Programmer when writing with Andy Hunt in 1999? What led him to challenge Agile commercialization? What principles guided Dave 'pragdave' Thomas when this conversation was recorded? How do those lessons inform the software systems we design today?",
  "Roll archive footage (YouTube ID: 4Io6gcQcuVQ). Watch for the unvarnished hallway exchanges, the emphasis on craft over speed, and the sheer enthusiasm of engineers taking responsibility for their software.",
  "Rules that hardened twenty years ago must be re-evaluated. The spirit of the Pragmatic Programmer is experimentation, not orthodoxy. When implementation is cheap, verification and clarity become everything. We cannot accept the mirage of competence. Let us examine the terminal contracts directly.",
  "Thank you for joining today's session. Full transcripts, provenance notes, and companion research are available at just3ws.com. In our next broadcast, we explore Episode 18. Until next time, keep your feedback loops fast and your code humane."
]